**The `sweep_holds` loop has two intertwined bugs:**

1. **Index-skip-on-erase.** `for (i=0; ...) { ...; queue_.erase(begin()+i); ...; }` then `i++`. After erasing slot `i`, the element at `i+1` slides down into `i`, but the `i++` skips straight past it. Two *adjacent* lapsed holds → the second is never examined. That's exactly why T-103's neighbor T-104 survives the minute-40 sweep, why only 2 of 3 are reported dropped, and why the all-adjacent run `[T-201..T-204]` drops only T-201 and T-203.

